    "summary": "This 1918 Ahrens-Fox M-K-4 is a pump-and-hose fire truck that was delivered new to the Mount Vernon Fire Department in Westchester County, New York, for which it served until being retired in the early 1950s. Truck number 858 is said to have been traded to the Seagrave Corporation and passed through the hands of a racehorse trader before being purchased in 1953 by the fire chief of the Branford, Connecticut, fire department. Its stewardship was later passed to the fire chief’s son, who commissioned its refurbishment and retained the truck until his 2023 passing. Finished in red with gold and black accents, the truck is equipped with a 998ci T-head inline-six that powers the rear wheels via a three-speed manual transmission and a chain-drive rear axle as well as a front-mounted four-piston water pump. The chassis has been fitted with 20\" painted steel wheels with pneumatic tires in lieu of the original artillery wheels with solid-rubber tires. Additional features include a chrome spherical air chamber, a bench seat upholstered in black leather, mechanically actuated dual rear brakes, triple discharge and dual intake connections, a chemical tank, a hose reel, wood ladders, a pike pole, and period brass hand-held extinguishers. Purchased by the selling dealer in 2023, this Ahrens-Fox fire engine is now offered in St. Louis, Missouri, with a clean Montana title.",
    "image": "https://bringatrailer.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/DSC_9959-scaled-94222.jpg?w=940",
